               <code>
                  <coding>
                     <system value="http://loinc.org"/>
                     <code value="8648-8"/>
                     <display value="Hospital course note"/>
                  </coding>
               </code>
               <text>
                  <status value="generated"/>
                  <div xmlns="http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml">Dear colleague, I am writing to inform you about the hospital stay of your 86-year-old male patient, admitted on 27/10/2020 due to an acute exacerbation of his known Chronic Obstructive Pulmonary Disease (COPD). On admission, the patient presented with increased dyspnoea, productive cough, and reduced oxygen saturation. Chest X-ray and arterial blood gas analysis were performed, confirming acute exacerbation without signs of pneumonia. Spirometry supported the known obstructive pattern. Treatment consisted of inhaled short-acting bronchodilators (salbutamol, ipratropium), systemic corticosteroids (prednisolone), and controlled oxygen therapy. The patient responded well, with significant clinical improvement. He was discharged on 28/10/2020 in stable condition. I recommend continuation of optimised inhaler therapy and close outpatient follow-up. Please do not hesitate to contact me for further information.</div>
               </text>
            </section>
